\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The evaluated settings, plotted. No regimes, and one line, which is a measurement.} X-axis: persistence $\gamma $. Y-axis: best single-defense ASR ($p_\text  {eff}$). Each marker is a setting we ran and carries its own measured value; the dotted line is the measured FL persistence $\hat  \gamma \approx 0.66$. \textbf  {An earlier version shaded four regime bands and drew threshold guides at $\gamma {=}0.15$, $p_\text  {eff}{=}0.3$ and $p_\text  {eff}{=}0.6$; none of those numbers was measured, so all six are gone.} Five points cannot locate a boundary, and nothing here is evidence of a phase transition in $(\gamma , p_\text  {eff})$ space.}}{32}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:regime}{{7}{32}{\textbf {The evaluated settings, plotted. No regimes, and one line, which is a measurement.} X-axis: persistence $\gamma $. Y-axis: best single-defense ASR ($p_\text {eff}$). Each marker is a setting we ran and carries its own measured value; the dotted line is the measured FL persistence $\hat \gamma \approx 0.66$. \textbf {An earlier version shaded four regime bands and drew threshold guides at $\gamma {=}0.15$, $p_\text {eff}{=}0.3$ and $p_\text {eff}{=}0.6$; none of those numbers was measured, so all six are gone.} Five points cannot locate a boundary, and nothing here is evidence of a phase transition in $(\gamma , p_\text {eff})$ space}{figure.7}{}}
